==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|p|ä}}

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Uralic|päŋe|lang=fi}}. Cognates include Estonian {{term|pea}}, Veps {{term|pä}} and Hungarian {{term|fej}}, {{term|fő}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/pæː/}}
* {{rhymes|æː|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|pää}}

===Noun===
{{infl|fi|noun}}

# [[head]] (of an organism or organisation)
# [[end]], [[tip]] (physical end)

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-voi|pä|ä|ä}}

====Derived terms====
* [[käydä päinsä|käydä ''päin''sä]] (''instructive pl.'' + ''possessive suffix'') = to [[do]], [[be]] [[acceptable]]
* [[ahtaa]] ''päähä[[-nsä|nsä]]'' = to [[cram]] (''information, into one's head''), [[study]] [[hard]]
* ''inessive'' + [[ei#Finnish|ei]] + [[olla#Finnish|3rd-pers. sg. of ''olla'']] + ''päätä'' [[ei#Finnish|ei]][[-kä|kä]] [[häntä]]ä = [[cannot]] be [[made]] [[head]]s or [[tail]]s of.
*:* ''[[tämä|Tässä]] [[ei#Finnish|ei]] [[ole#Finnish|ole]] '''päätä''' [[eikä]] [[häntä]]ä.''
*:** ''I '''can't make heads or tails of this'''. / This '''makes no sense'''. / This '''is totally [[preposterous]].'''''
